#  What a checkout is allowed to change, and what it is not.
#
#  Git on Windows converts line endings on checkout. For source that is
#  read, that is harmless. For a file the KERNEL executes it is fatal and
#  silent: docker-entrypoint.sh checked out with CRLF has a shebang
#  reading "/bin/sh\r", and the container dies with
#
#      exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
#  which names the file it just failed to find. The repository stored LF
#  all along -- the damage happened between clone and build, so it could
#  only ever be seen by building a CLONE rather than the tree it was
#  authored in. A Linux host never converts and never sees it; anyone on
#  Windows gets an image that cannot start.
* text=auto

#  Anything executed, in the container or out of it, keeps Unix endings
#  on every platform.
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

#  And nothing gets to guess about these.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
